{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 25, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**A Most Wondrous Itinerary for a Voyage to the Land of the Rising Sun**\n\n*Act I: The Dawn of Arrival*\n\n**Scene I: The Imperial City of Tokyo**\n\nFirst to the bustling wards of Edo’s fair metropolis do thou proceed. Therein the grand Shibuya Crossing doth call like a siren’s song. Mark well the towering Shibuya 109 whose lights do flash like stars in mortal guise. Spend thy first eve in the ways of Shinjuku where neon signs and izakayas do abound.\n\n**Scene II: The Castle of the Shogun**\n\nUpon the morrow venture forth to the castle of Edo which now doth stand as but a shadow of its former might. Yet still the gardens of the East Garden do offer respite from the city’s ceaseless hum. There let thy spirit wander among the stones and streams that tell of ancient days.\n\n*Act II: The Path to the Ancient Capital*\n\n**Scene III: The Journey to Kyoto**\n\nWith haste board the famed Shinkansen whose speed is as swift as Cupid’s arrow. Two hours hence thou shalt find thyself in the heart of the old imperial seat—Kyoto the fair.\n\n**Scene IV: Temples and Tea Houses**\n\nIn Kyoto’s embrace let thy soul be nourished. First to the golden Kinkaku-ji do thou repair whose topmost floors gleam like the sun itself. Then to the bamboo groves of Arashiyama where the wind doth whisper through the stalks like players in some grand masquerade.\n\nLet not the day pass without a visit to the Fushimi Inari Shrine where torii gates do climb the mountain like a crimson river. And when the sun doth dip below the horizon repair to a humble tea house where the matcha is whipped to froth as fair as any courtier’s plume.\n\n*Act III: The Spirit of Nara*\n\n**Scene V: The Ancient Deer Park**\n\nUpon the morn take thy leave of Kyoto and journey to Nara the ancient. There the great Todai-ji doth stand a testament to faith and craft. Mark well the Buddha whose gaze doth follow thee as thou dost walk. And in the park where deer do roam like lords of the manor let them bow their heads for treats of sacred mochi.\n\n*Act IV: The Floating World of Osaka*\n\n**Scene VI: The Merchant’s Pride**\n\nFrom Nara’s gentle slopes make haste to Osaka the merchant’s jewel. There the castle of the great Toyotomi doth rise once more in grandeur though rebuilt by hands of modern cunning. Let thy tongue delight in the takoyaki and okonomiyaki of Dotonbori where the river doth run with the glow of a thousand lanterns.\n\n*Act V: The Return to Tokyo and Farewell*\n\n**Scene VII: The Final Days**\n\nWith heavy heart but lightened purse return to the ways of Tokyo. Spend thy last days in the elegance of Ginza where the shops do gleam with treasures rare. Or in the verdant embrace of Ueno Park where the cherry blossoms may linger still if fortune favors thee.\n\n**Scene VIII: The Parting of Ways**\n\nUpon thy final night let a ryokan be thy lodging where the tatami doth cushion thy repose and the onsen doth cleanse thy spirit. There let the hot waters carry away the dust of thy travels and prepare thee for the long journey home.\n\nThus ends thy sojourn in the land of the Rising Sun. Go forth with memory as thy guide and may the gods of Japan smile upon thy path.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.45995622873306274}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.06741323322057724}, {"token": " Most", "logprob": -0.6492467522621155}, {"token": " W", "logprob": -0.6890980005264282}, {"token": "ond", "logprob": -1.168244216387393e-05}, {"token": "rous", "logprob": -6.437280717364047e-06}, {"token": " It", "logprob": -0.24275867640972137}, {"token": "iner", "logprob": -0.0003909300430677831}, {"token": "ary", "logprob": -0.002532372483983636}, {"token": " for", "logprob": -0.0447256900370121}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.14415408670902252}, {"token": " Voyage", "logprob": -3.914280414581299}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.0173320434987545}, {"token": " the", "l